id: flooding-technique
name: Flooding Technique
uaType: magical
prerequisite: N/A
tpCost: 15
type: standard
actionCost: 2
kiCostPerBaseTier: 6
# Applied when used, never again while it is (use-maneuver.mjs askSustain); its KP paid at the start of each of your
# turns with a Stop on the card, ended if it cannot be (chat.mjs upkeepUniques); "Applied" on its row ends it as an
# Instant. The Large Sphere is said on the card.
sustained: true
instantRelease: true
sphereMagnitude: large
# "The Battle Environment becomes Underwater": yours, for you stand at the centre and it moves with you - the one you
# had kept and given back when it ends. Whoever else is inside sets their own on the Battlefields tab (the table's).
floods: underwater-environment
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Large Sphere around you, and moving with you, becomes Underwater - yours set; its KP again at the start of each of
  your turns, or it ends; ended as an Instant. Passive: Combat Rolls 1(T) higher Underwater.
text: >
  Flooding Technique: You can magically produce enough water to change the tides of battle, creating an ocean on the
  battlefield.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –TP Cost: 15
  –KP Cost: 6(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 2 Actions
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: While in the Underwater Battle Environment, increase your Combat Rolls by 1(T).
  –Effect: Within a Large Sphere AoE (centered on you), the Battle Environment becomes Underwater. If you move to
  another Square due to any effect, the AoE containing this Battle Environment moves the exact same distance and in the
  same direction.

  You cannot use this Unique Ability while it is active, and must pay the Ki Point Cost of this Unique Ability at the
  start of each of your turns or return the Battle Environment to what it would normally be. You may return the Battle
  Environment to normal as an Instant Action.

---

# "While in the Underwater Battle Environment" - yours, and not while you are above it in a High Environment.
[passive]
if (inEnvironment("underwater")) {
  combatRolls += 1(T);
}
